---
source: crates/hibi-cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "help(&repo, &[command, \"--help\"])"
---
$ hibi list --help
exit status: 0
---- standard output ----
Read the store and print claims as they are stored. Nothing is resolved and no state is computed, so this works when files or providers are missing.

Without an id: one line per live claim. With an id: the stored claim, its marks in time order and its retirement.

Usage: hibi list [OPTIONS] [claim-id]

Arguments:
  [claim-id]
          Show this claim as stored, with its marks and retirement. May be shortened to a unique prefix

Options:
      --loc <glob>
          Keep a claim only when the locator of one of its sides matches this glob. Repeat for several

      --text <substring>
          Keep a claim only when its statement contains this text. The match is case-sensitive

      --retired
          Include retired claims

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --root <dir>
          Use this directory as the root (the directory that contains .hibi/) instead of searching upward from the working directory

      --format <format>
          Output format. Without this option the output is JSON when standard output is not a terminal, and text when it is

          Possible values:
          - human: Text for a person
          - json:  One JSON object

      --now <timestamp>
          Use this instant as the current time, for reproducible runs. RFC 3339 with any offset, for example 2026-11-20T18:04:11Z. A fraction of a second is dropped

      --no-cache
          Do not read or write the cache database. Results are the same with and without the cache
---- standard error ----
(empty)
